rming gestures  are all he knows i baptize you in the  name of the Father and of the Son and of  the Holy Spirit  suddenly the choirs in the congregation  are gone leaving only a lonely live  stream however these are different times  and different circumstances in his  province Newfoundland and Labrador most  covered 19 cases have been traced to a  single funeral home gathering funerals  and wakes are banned no more than five  people are permitted at a burial even in  formal processions have been shut down  because people started gathering in  groups on the roadside when I see a  family at the graveside my initial  instinct is to you know either to extend  a hand to say you know I'm sorry for  your loss or you know if you know  someone even on it you know a closer  basis to offer a hug and at this time  we're just not allowed to do that and  and you wrestle with it you struggle  with it and at times you hate yourself  because you're not able to do it it's  not only grieving this restricted  distancing rules are stifling those  once-in-a-lifetime moments like first  time grandparents touching a precious  newborn and when I found out that none  of us could see him none of us could go  in and everything it was just like this  won't be happening this just can't be  happening and they took out of this over  the car in his kursi bumped him on the  driveway and said okay you can't come  any closer  for now they'll get by watching videos  of their grandson Nico emerging into  this world those suffering apart from  loved ones who are dying faced a much  more excruciating ordeal if you're  grieving know that you're not alone we  are here for you Sophia loss in ski is  finding ways to remember her brother  I have Anthony with me right now these  are his gloves and we're holding each  other's hands even  he's not here he's he's with me every  single day she wants desperately for her  entire family to mark her brother's  death and scatter his ashes together  we're gonna hold eac